Prefix Sum
      Precompute cumulative totals in an array to answer any contiguous range sum query in $O(1)$ time.
      LC 862

Fenwick Tree
      Utilize bitwise index relations to support both point updates 
      and prefix sum queries in Log-N time with a lightweight, flat array structure.
      LC 315

Segment Tree
      Build a full binary tree structure to support flexible range queries (Min, Max, GCD) 
      and dynamic array updates in Log-N time.
      LC 699

Sentinel Node / Value
      Introduce dummy boundaries (like a fake tail node or infinity limits) to eliminate conditional branch checking in loops.
      LC 84

Lazy Deletion
      Postpone the overhead of physically removing invalid elements from a data structure (like a Heap) until they naturally 
      surface at the top during queries.
      LC 871

Relaxation
      Repeatedly check if an intermediate path can shrink the currently known shortest distance to a vertex, 
      updating it if a more optimal option exists.
      LC 787

Edge Chaining (Hashing)
      Address hash map collision conflicts by storing intersecting keys within a linked list 
      chain at the same bucket location.
      LC 706

Catalan Number
      Evaluate the total unique combinations of structurally balanced formations (like valid parenthesizations or full binary trees)
      LC 96

Ackermann Function
      A classic, non-primitive recursive mathematical function used to establish bounds on structural growth 
      rates (such as the inverse Ackermann function $\alpha(n)$ used in Union-Find time analysis)

Fence Post Problem
      Avoid classic off-by-one errors by recognizing that connecting $N$ items in a sequence always requires 
      exactly $N-1$ connectors or separators.
      LC 1096

