Locks / Mutex (Mutual Exclusion)
      Restrict code execution blocks so that only a single thread can interact with a resource, 
      forcing all other threads to block and wait.
      LC 1114

Segmented Locking (Striping)
      Divide a giant data structure into independent shards, assigning distinct locks to each piece to let multiple threads 
      modify different regions simultaneously.
      LC 146

Semaphore
      Use a counter-based variable to control thread access, enabling a designated maximum number of concurrent threads 
      to share a fixed pool of resource instances.
      LC 1117

RLock (Reentrant Lock)
      Allow a thread that already holds a specific lock to acquire it again without deadlocking itself, 
      matching nesting recursive function loops.

RWLock (Read-Write Lock)
      Allow multiple reader threads to access a resource concurrently, but completely block everyone when a writer thread requests 
      exclusive access to make an update.
      LC 1242
